            "zh": "搁浅"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " near South America. The iceberg is called A23a. It started moving away from Antarctica and was "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " toward an island called South Georgia. Scientists were "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " it might hit the island and "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the penguins and seals living there. But instead, it stopped about 50 miles away."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "A23a is very big—about "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "twice",
            "zh": "两倍"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of Houston, Texas! It broke off from Antarctica a long time ago, in 1986, and "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in the cold sea for 30 years. Then in 2020, it began to "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "float",
            "zh": "漂浮"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " north. Last year, it "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "spun",
            "zh": "旋转"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " around in the ocean for months before moving toward South Georgia again."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Now, scientists think A23a will "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " into smaller "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "pieces",
            "ref": "v-piece"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and melt. When it melts, it can help sea life because the ice has "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "nutrients",
            "zh": "营养物质"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " that make the ocean "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But if it breaks apart too much, ships may need to change their "
          },
          {
